# The context of the module lib: it works out the total of an order, and publishes the rule that
# does, whose output `total` its term means. The rule applies the VAT rate of the module base, which
# has rules and no context of its own, so this context owns that rule too (`@base/…`, a path from
# the root of this module): a map takes a file of a dependency in when a context of the map owns it.
context Pricing(pricing) v1
description "Works out the total of an order: its subtotal, the VAT of its category and the shipping fee"
owner "Pricing team"

owns
  rulec "../rules/order_total.rule"
  rulec "@base/rules/vat_rate.rule"

published language rulec.order_total.v1
  rulec "../rules/order_total.rule"

terms
  total "What the customer pays for an order: its subtotal, the VAT of its category and the shipping fee"
    means rulec "../rules/order_total.rule" output total
